# SHA-256 of every upstream file this SDK ships unmodified, taken from the two
# official SQLite 3.53.4 release archives unpacked into this repository:
#
#   src/      sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip   4 files
#   upstream/ sqlite-src-3530400.zip           10 files
#   test/     sqlite-src-3530400.zip         1285 files
#
# Release: SQLite 3.53.4, 2026-07-24, Fossil check-in
# bf7c7f30031888f4e796e429ab3978879485813aaca6f641c7b33e4e09459bcc
# (`upstream/manifest.uuid`, and `src/sqlite3.h:151`'s SQLITE_SOURCE_ID).
# The tag is `version-3.53.4` (`upstream/manifest.tags`), the branch
# `branch-3.53` (`src/sqlite3.h:152`).
#
# 1299 records: 4 under src/, 10 under upstream/, 1285 under test/. That is the
# complete file list of both archives as unpacked here, so a dependent receives
# the upstream project rather than a hand-picked subset of it. Nothing is
# dropped for size and nothing is dropped for being uncompiled: the 1285-file TCL
# suite travels whole even though `zig build` runs none of it (build.zig says
# what running it would require and why this graph does not have that closure).
#
# The sha256 of each *archive* is NOT recorded in this tree and is therefore not
# claimed here. No copy of sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip or
# sqlite-src-3530400.zip is present to hash, and an unobserved digest is not an
# identifier this file may state. What is verifiable here is every individual
# file, which is what this list is. See UPSTREAM.md, "The release archives' own
# digests are not in this tree".
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from the repository root checks the bytes.
# tools/check-provenance.sh additionally rejects a missing, extra or renamed file
# under src/, upstream/ or test/, which a plain checksum run cannot see, and
# cross-checks the vendored bytes against upstream's own Fossil manifest where
# that manifest names the file.
#
